            "text": "{\"description\":\"The visible carved surface shows a tall rounded stone form with shallow incised lines and raised/eroded relief. Near the upper middle there are faint vertical and curved marks; across the midsection there are several small circular or oval depressions and a clearer circular ring, with broad curved band-like arcs below. The lower surface is mostly plain and worn, with one small oval mark near the bottom.\",\"avian\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"There are faint irregular incisions on the upper and middle surface, but no clearly readable bird body or distinct birdlike head/beak can be identified from the visible carving alone.\",\"box\":null},\"large_face\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"No large front or oblique human face with eyes, nose, and mouth is visible on the main carved surface; the visible marks are mostly abstract lines, circles, and arcs.\",\"box\":null},\"scorpion\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"Some faint curving and branching lines appear on the midsection, but legs and a segmented upturned tail are not clearly legible.\",\"box\":null},\"round_motif\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"A distinct carved circular ring is visible near the center of the stone surface, separate from facial features or repair marks.\",\"box\":[0.395,0.543,0.514,0.625]},\"three_arches\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"There are broad repeated curved bands across the lower middle, but they do not clearly form three separate arch-topped forms side by side.\",\"box\":null},\"limitations\":\"The stone is heavily worn and unevenly lit, with shallow eroded carving and surface texture making many lines ambiguous; background objects were ignored.\"}",
